WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.341 --> 00:00:03.210
(eerie chiming music)

00:00:03.210 --> 00:00:07.377
- Faces are the most important
subject matter in art.

00:00:10.140 --> 00:00:14.220
It's a never-ending source of material.

00:00:14.220 --> 00:00:16.061
When you put on one of my masks,

00:00:16.061 --> 00:00:19.379
you become somebody different.

00:00:19.379 --> 00:00:22.350
You start to embody that character,

00:00:22.350 --> 00:00:24.850
and have a lot of fun with it.

00:00:30.148 --> 00:00:32.418
My name's Landon Meier and I make

00:00:32.418 --> 00:00:34.835
disturbingly realistic masks.

00:00:36.789 --> 00:00:40.816
(bouncy, playful music)

00:00:40.816 --> 00:00:44.456
I never thought I was gonna
make a living doing masks.

00:00:44.456 --> 00:00:46.744
I was a picture framer, loan officer,

00:00:46.744 --> 00:00:50.661
pizza delivery driver,
and then I got laid off.

00:00:51.706 --> 00:00:53.704
I've always been interested
in doing something

00:00:53.704 --> 00:00:56.936
that's really surreal and nightmarish.

00:00:56.936 --> 00:01:01.103
So, it was more or less an
experiment that took off.

00:01:02.595 --> 00:01:04.733
I am the only person
out there that's doing

00:01:04.733 --> 00:01:07.691
hyper-realistic likeness masks.

00:01:07.691 --> 00:01:10.758
I'm kind of this weird mad scientist

00:01:10.758 --> 00:01:12.508
down in the basement.

00:01:15.870 --> 00:01:19.787
I start off getting lots
of reference material.

00:01:21.055 --> 00:01:23.902
The hardest part is doing the sculpture.

00:01:23.902 --> 00:01:27.059
That can take anywhere
from four days to a year,

00:01:27.059 --> 00:01:29.611
but once the sculpt is
done and I have a mold,

00:01:29.611 --> 00:01:33.361
it's about a one week
process to make a mask.

00:01:35.309 --> 00:01:37.427
They are ungodly expensive.

00:01:37.427 --> 00:01:41.594
They range $500 and up, and
sometimes even high as $7,500.

00:01:43.756 --> 00:01:47.718
Over the years I've made
approximately 25 different designs,

00:01:47.718 --> 00:01:51.885
and I've produced with my
own hands over 1,000 masks.

00:01:56.476 --> 00:02:00.150
What I make, I like to
consider wearable art.

00:02:00.150 --> 00:02:03.745
These are super realistic
sculptures you can

00:02:03.745 --> 00:02:06.789
put over your head and wear.

00:02:06.789 --> 00:02:10.523
People just seem to have
this astonished reaction

00:02:10.523 --> 00:02:14.106
to the masks, that's
what I love about 'em.

00:02:18.769 --> 00:02:20.936
(chiming)

